adjudication.rationale:
The diff adds a strict string comparison:

```py
if pipeline.fetch_state("github_authenticated_user") != integration.metadata["sender"]["login"]:
    return error(...)
```

There’s no normalization (e.g., `.lower()`/`.casefold()`) on either side. If GitHub can represent the same username with different casing across the OAuth `/user` response vs the stored webhook `sender.login`, this check could reject an otherwise legitimate installation flow. The diff itself shows the comparison is case-sensitive; whether GitHub logins can differ by case isn’t proven within the diff, so it’s best treated as a robustness/edge-case concern rather than a clearly verifiable defect.
